From: realazizk <azizk@tuta.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 13:42:37 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] screenshare: a new frame of a stopped output session has
 no monitor transform

A client can send ext_image_copy_capture_session_v1.create_frame before it
reads the session's `stopped`: the protocol answers such a frame with
failed(stopped). When the session stopped because its output was removed,
CImageCopyCaptureFrame's constructor sends CScreenshareFrame::transform(),
which read the null monitor's transform and crashed (SIGSEGV,
ScreenshareFrame.cpp:513). It now reports the normal transform for a gone
monitor; capturing the frame fails with `stopped` (share() checks it).

Upstream main no longer reads the monitor here since #15714 ("render: always
render in normal transform"); that change depends on the render rewrite, so
0.56.2 gets only the null check.
---
 src/managers/screenshare/ScreenshareFrame.cpp | 10 +++++++++-
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/managers/screenshare/ScreenshareFrame.cpp b/src/managers/screenshare/ScreenshareFrame.cpp
index c74adcb..fcef499 100644
--- a/src/managers/screenshare/ScreenshareFrame.cpp
+++ b/src/managers/screenshare/ScreenshareFrame.cpp
@@ -508,9 +508,17 @@ Vector2D CScreenshareFrame::bufferSize() const {
 }
 
 wl_output_transform CScreenshareFrame::transform() const {
+    if (m_session.expired())
+        return WL_OUTPUT_TRANSFORM_NORMAL;
+
     switch (m_session->m_type) {
         case SHARE_REGION:
-        case SHARE_MONITOR: return m_session->monitor()->m_transform;
+        case SHARE_MONITOR: {
+            // a frame created after the monitor went (the session is stopped; capturing it fails
+            // with `stopped`) has no transform to report
+            const auto PMONITOR = m_session->monitor();
+            return PMONITOR ? PMONITOR->m_transform : WL_OUTPUT_TRANSFORM_NORMAL;
+        }
         default:
         case SHARE_WINDOW: return WL_OUTPUT_TRANSFORM_NORMAL;
     }
